              <h2>The 7 Best Nature &amp; Animal Apps for Children</h2>

              <!-- 1. KIDAMAME DISCOVERY -->
              <div class="app-review-card kidamame-pick">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill"><i class="fa-solid fa-earth-americas"></i> Best Calm Biome &amp;
                      Wildlife Explorer (Ages 4–10)</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">1. Kidamame Discovery</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-infinity"></i> One-Time Purchase (No Subscription)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-paw"></i> 120+ Interactive Elements &amp; ~400 Facts</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-plane-departure"></i> 100% Offline</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <strong><a href="/discovery/">Kidamame Discovery</a></strong> is a calm, Montessori-inspired digital
                  picture book where the natural world comes alive at your child's fingertips. Designed for kids ages
                  4–10 and their families, it replaces noisy timers and points with pure, child-led exploration across
                  <strong>6 rich ecosystems</strong>:
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>The Alps, African Savannah, Australian Outback, The Arctic, Sonoran Desert, and Amazon
                      Rainforest:</strong> Each scene contains <strong>20 or more interactive animals, plants, and
                      natural phenomena</strong> (120+ in total).</li>
                  <li><strong>Authentic Sounds &amp; Gentle Animations:</strong> Tap the ostrich to see its eggs tumble,
                    touch the volcano to watch an eruption, or watch a glacier calve into the sea while listening to
                    authentic wildlife calls and ambient forest sounds.</li>
                  <li><strong>Around 400 "Did You Know?" Cards:</strong> Tapping the magnifying glass reveals
                    illustrated science facts in 6 languages (English, Italian, French, German, Spanish, and Portuguese)
                    that are genuinely fascinating for both children and parents.</li>
                  <li><strong>100% Offline, No Ads, No Subscriptions:</strong> Try it for free and unlock the full app
                    forever with a single one-time purchase.</li>
                </ul>
                <%- include('../../partials/guide-kidamame-gallery') %>
              </div>

              <!-- 2. SEEK BY INATURALIST -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Outdoor Field Guide for Plants &amp; Bugs</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">2. Seek by iNaturalist</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 5–12+ (with Parent)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> 100% Free</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i> Zero Data Collection / No Login</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Created by a joint initiative of the California Academy of Sciences and the National Geographic
                  Society, <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/pages/seek_app" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Seek by iNaturalist</a> is the kid-safe companion to the global citizen
                  science platform iNaturalist. Point your device's camera at any wildflower, tree leaf, mushroom,
                  amphibian, or beetle on a family walk, and Seek identifies the species in real time using on-device
                  computer vision trained on millions of wildlife observations.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Seek turns every neighborhood stroll into a real-life treasure
                  hunt. Once a species is identified, children can read child-friendly facts about its taxonomy, range,
                  and seasonality, and earn optional nature badges. Best of all, it requires no registration and collects
                  zero personal or location data by default, making it one of the most trustworthy free apps a family can
                  download.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 3. MERLIN BIRD ID -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best for Listening to Real Birds Outdoors</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">3. Merlin Bird ID (by the Cornell Lab of Ornithology)
                    </h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 5–12+</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> 100% Free</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-microphone"></i> Live Bird Song ID</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Developed by the renowned Cornell Lab of Ornithology, <a href="https://www.merlinbirds.org/download/"
                    target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Merlin Bird ID</a> is a non-profit masterpiece whose
                  "Sound ID" feature feels like pure magic to children and adults alike. Tap record in your backyard, on
                  a balcony, or in a local park, and the app displays live spectrograms while lighting up photos of
                  every bird species singing around you in real time.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Beyond Sound ID, Merlin includes a simple three-question bird
                  identification wizard (size, colors, and behavior) and downloadable regional bird packs covering
                  thousands of species worldwide. It naturally encourages kids to stand still, stay quiet, and listen
                  closely to the living world around them.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 4. TINYBOP MAMMALS, PLANTS & CORAL REEF -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Series of Interactive Science &amp; Nature Models</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">4. Tinybop's Explorer's Library (Mammals, Plants, Coral
                      Reef &amp; More)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Standalone Purchases</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-bone"></i> Interactive Biology &amp; Earth Science</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Brooklyn-based studio <a href="https://tinybop.com/apps" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Tinybop</a> has created an entire library of open-ended, artist-illustrated
                  science apps. Their nature titles let children look beneath the surface of living things: in
                  <em>Mammals</em>, kids can peer inside a bat's skeleton as it flies, see how an elephant digests food,
                  or look inside a kangaroo's pouch as a joey grows.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Across their wider catalog (including <em>Coral Reef</em>,
                  <em>Plants</em>, <em>The Earth</em>, <em>Weather</em>, <em>Space</em>, and <em>The Human Body</em>),
                  children explore how entire ecosystems and natural forces interact, watching cleaner shrimp tend to sea
                  turtles or observing how seasons and wildfires shape forest habitats. Every app is unscored, unhurried,
                  and supported by free downloadable parent guides.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 5. TOCA NATURE -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best for Sculpting Landscapes &amp; Habitats</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">5. Toca Nature (in Toca Boca Jr)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–8</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Included in Toca Boca Jr</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-mountain-sun"></i> 3D Habitat Sandbox</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Originally released as a standalone classic and now included inside <a
                    href="https://www.tocaboca.com/toca-boca-jr" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Toca Boca Jr</a>, <em>Toca Nature</em> gives children a magical block of
                  earth to shape with their fingers. Raising mountains brings snow and wolves, digging valleys creates
                  lakes for beavers and fish, and planting different trees invites bears, foxes, woodpeckers, and deer.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Once a landscape comes alive, children can walk through their
                  forest from a ground-level magnifying view, observe animals sleeping by night and foraging by day, and
                  gather berries, mushrooms, and nuts to feed each species.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 6. WWF TOGETHER -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best for Older Kids Learning About Conservation</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">6. WWF Together</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 6–12</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> 100% Free</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-paw"></i> Endangered Wildlife</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Winner of an Apple Design Award and created by the <a
                    href="https://www.worldwildlife.org/resources/activities/educational-apps/wwf-together/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">World Wildlife Fund</a>, <em>WWF Together</em> brings older children
                  face-to-face with giant pandas, snow leopards, elephants, sea turtles, and monarch butterflies through
                  beautifully unfolding origami-inspired interactive stories.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Kids can swipe to see the world through "animal vision" camera
                  filters (like how a tiger or butterfly perceives color and motion), chop bamboo for pandas, and see
                  their real physical distance from each animal's habitat on a 3D globe. Each animal story even includes
                  a downloadable origami folding guide for hands-on craft time after putting the tablet down.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 7. ALBA: A WILDLIFE ADVENTURE -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Story-Driven Wildlife Adventure (Apple Arcade)</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">7. Alba: A Wildlife Adventure (by ustwo games)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 6–12+</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-apple-whole"></i> Apple Arcade (iPhone/iPad) &amp; Console</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-camera-retro"></i> Wildlife Photography</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Created by BAFTA-winning studio ustwo games (the team behind <em>Monument Valley</em>), <a
                    href="https://www.albawildlife.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Alba: A Wildlife
                    Adventure</a> follows a young girl visiting her grandparents on a sun-drenched Mediterranean island.
                  Armed with a field guide and a camera, children explore beaches, pine forests, and wetlands to
                  photograph over 60 real bird and animal species, clean up litter, and save the local nature reserve.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> On mobile and tablet, <em>Alba</em> is available exclusively
                  through Apple Arcade (as well as Nintendo Switch and PC), meaning it has zero ads and zero
                  microtransactions. It is a heartfelt, gentle adventure that leaves children inspired to care for local
                  wildlife in their own community.
                </p>
              </div>

